{
  "$comment": [
    "Every multipart curl example on Photoroom's Image Editing and Remove Background docs pages, as published.",
    "Extracted mechanically on 2026-11-24 from the `.md` rendering of each page listed in https://docs.photoroom.com/llms.txt under image-editing-api-plus-plan/ and remove-background-api-basic-plan/: one entry per fenced `curl` block that posts form fields to a photoroom.com URL.",
    "`fields` are the `--form` / `-F` arguments as curl sends them: shell quoting removed, and the double quotes curl itself strips from a quoted value (`--form 'referenceBox=\"originalImage\"'`) removed too. Form values are text on the wire. A file argument (`name=@/path`) is recorded as \"@file\". `headers` are the `--header` lines other than `x-api-key` and `accept`.",
    "Read by src/providers/photoroom/*.test.ts, which asserts that every one of these validates with no error and no warning: a validator that objects to the provider's own documentation is wrong."
  ],
